{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790423085356,"sessionID":"ses_f227a2f15ffebGWYEOArrs0iMx","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_171ad90f1a324d40bbe3dcee","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore project structure","subagent_type":"explore","prompt":"Explore the /workspace project structure quickly. Read project.godot, any scene files, and scripts to understand how the TileSet and tiles are used. Also check task_config.json. Return all relevant information about how tiles are used, what tile shape is configured, and any existing terrain or autotile configuration."},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f22796ef6ffeyDavxjCLfB0NPI\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is a comprehensive summary of all findings about the project structure, TileSet, and tiles.\n\n---\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n/workspace/\n  .godot/\n    .gdignore\n    editor/\n      filesystem_cache10\n      main.tscn-folding-*.cfg\n      project_metadata.cfg\n    imported/\n    global_script_class_cache.cfg\n    scene_groups_cache.cfg\n    uid_cache.bin\n  assets/\n    sprites/\n      tile_iso.png          <-- Primary sprite sheet used by the TileSet\n      simple_tileset.png    <-- Unused in any resource/source\n      tilemap.png           <-- Unused in any resource/source\n    tile_set.tres           <-- The sole TileSet resource\n  scenes/\n    main.tscn               <-- Main scene\n  scripts/                  <-- Empty (no .gd scripts in the project)\n  project.godot\n  task_config.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## Project Configuration (`project.godot`)\n\n| Key | Value |\n|-----|-------|\n| Godot version | 4.5 (config_version=5, features=[\"4.5\"]) |\n| Project name | \"Place Asset at Origin\" |\n| Main scene | `res://scenes/main.tscn` |\n| Renderer | `gl_compatibility` |\n| Default clear color | `(0.649, 0.814, 0.954, 1.0)` (light blue) |\n\n---\n\n## Scripts\n\n**There are zero GDScript files** in the project (`/workspace/scripts/` is empty, and a glob for `**/*.gd` returned no results). This is a purely visual/scene-based project with no code logic.\n\n---\n\n## Scene (`scenes/main.tscn`)\n\n- **Root**: `Node2D` named `\"Main\"`\n  - **`Node2D` named `\"TileMap\"`** -- parent container for tile layers\n    - **`TileMapLayer` named `\"Base\"`** -- uses `tile_set` (res://assets/tile_set.tres), has `texture_filter = 1` (nearest), `use_parent_material = true`. Contains a large `tile_map_data` binary blob with many tile placements.\n    - **`TileMapLayer` named `\"Deco\"`** -- uses the same `tile_set`. Contains only 4 tile placements (a sparse decoration layer).\n  - **`Camera2D`** -- positioned at (284, 162), zoom level 2x.\n\n---\n\n## TileSet Resource (`assets/tile_set.tres`) -- Primary Focus\n\n### Top-Level Resource Properties\n\n| Property | Value |\n|----------|-------|\n| `tile_shape` | **`2`** (Half-Offset Square) |\n| `tile_size` | `Vector2i(28, 18)` |\n| `sources/1` | `TileSetAtlasSource` (single atlas source) |\n| Terrain sets | **None defined** (no `terrain_0/...` entries in the `[resource]` section) |\n| Navigation layer 0 | Enabled (`layers = 1`) |\n| Physics layer 0 | Collision layer = 1 |\n\n### Atlas Source (`TileSetAtlasSource_ki5qi`)\n\n- **Texture**: `res://assets/sprites/tile_iso.png`\n- **Texture region size**: `Vector2i(45, 20)` (each individual tile in the sprite sheet is 45x20 pixels)\n- **Tiles defined**: 22 individual tiles, spread across coordinate grid positions (column:row):\n  \n  | Row | Columns | Tile Count |\n  |-----|---------|------------|\n  | 0 | 0, 1, 2, 3 | 4 |\n  | 1 | 0, 1, 2, 3 | 4 |\n  | 2 | 0, 1, 2, 3 | 4 |\n  | 3 | 0, 1, 2, 3 | 4 |\n  | 4 | 0, 1, 2 | 3 |\n  | 5 | 0, 1 | 2 |\n  | 6 | 0, 1 | 2 |\n  | 7 | 0, 1 | 2 |\n  | 8 | 0 | 1 |\n  | **Total** | | **26 individual tile entries** |\n\n### Per-Tile Configuration\n\nEvery tile in the atlas has the following properties set:\n\n- **`/terrain`**: Set to **`0`** on every tile (this is the terrain index). However, this is **not a functional terrain set assignment** -- there is no terrain set defined in the `[resource]` section of the TileSet, so the `terrain` value on tiles is orphaned/inert. It appears to be a default/placeholder.\n- **`/probability`**: Set to `0.25` on tiles `0:3`, `1:3`, and `0:4` (randomized tile variants). All others use the default probability.\n- **`/navigation_layer_0/polygon`**: Each tile has a navigation polygon assigned. Two shape patterns are used:\n  - **4-vertex rectangle** (`SubResource(\"NavigationPolygon_eslq1\")`, `_ki5qi`, `_u4lx5`, `_u6000`): vertices at (14,9), (-14,9), (-14,-9), (14,-9) -- a simple bounding rectangle for full/whole tiles.\n  - **6-vertex shaped polygon** (all other `NavigationPolygon_*` sub-resources): vertices at (14,9), (0,9), (-14,9), (-14,-9), (0,-9), (14,-9) -- an inset/offset polygon shape likely matching half-offset tile geometry.\n\n---\n\n## Terrain/Autotile Status\n\n**There is currently NO terrain set configured.** The TileSet resource section has no `terrain_set_0/mode`, `terrain_set_0/terrains_0/name`, or any similar terrain definition. The `terrain = 0` property on individual tiles is present in the atlas source entries but is non-functional without a proper terrain set definition in the resource section.\n\n---\n\n## Task (`task_config.json`)\n\nThe task instruction is:\n\n> Update `res://assets/tile_set.tres` to add a terrain set for the half-offset square tileset. Create a terrain set in **Match Corners** mode with a single terrain named **`Path`**; the terrain set uses the dirt path tiles against grass default. Configure all terrain peer bits correctly so all the **15 path tiles** autotile properly (include grass as default and **ignore the bordered path tile** in the tileset, which should be unused in this autotile). **Do not change the existing tile shape or other metadata.**\n\nKey points from this instruction:\n1. A terrain set must be **added** (it does not exist today).\n2. **Match Corners** mode (not Match Sides).\n3. One terrain named **`Path`**.\n4. The default (no path) is **grass** -- the empty/default terrain.\n5. **15 path tiles** need their terrain peer bits configured.\n6. The **bordered path tile** in the tileset should be **excluded/ignored** (unused in autotile).\n7. Tile shape (`tile_shape = 2`, Half-Offset Square) must **not** be changed.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f227a2f15ffebGWYEOArrs0iMx","sessionId":"ses_f22796ef6ffeyDavxjCLfB0NPI","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore project structure","time":{"start":1790422978828,"end":1790423085347}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_c17ed425-b740-46ff-aa83-a89043d234ec"}},"id":"prt_0dd869105001iIia1kBGl7ZTTF","sessionID":"ses_f227a2f15ffebGWYEOArrs0iMx","messageID":"msg_0dd860afb001PTxQp4IHcXeKH4"}}
